course: dictionary
lesson: 2660
title: Device: a machine or a clever trick
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A device is a machine or tool made for a special job. Your phone, a tablet and a can opener are all devices. In «Put your devices away at dinner», devices means phones and tablets, because they are things you can put away.
explain: Use the words around the word to find its meaning. In «Charging devices outside the bedroom removes the temptation to play at night», charging tells you a device runs on power. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Device has a second meaning: a clever way or trick used to get a result. In English lessons a «literary device» is a writing trick, such as a simile. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is meant.
fact: A device is a machine or tool made for a special job.
fact: «Devices» can mean phones, tablets and computers.
fact: A literary device is a writing trick, such as a simile.
fact: A server is a computer that provides things like web pages, videos or games; your own device is called the client.
fact: «Leave someone to their own devices» means let them do what they like.
exercise: What is a device? | A type of weather | A word for a sad song | *A machine or tool made for a special job | A kind of plant that grows in water
exercise: «Never use mains electrical things near a full bath or sink, because a device falling in can electrocute the person in the water.» What is a device in this sentence? | *An electrical machine or thing | A sponge | A bathtub | A small fish
exercise: In English lessons, a «literary device» is | *A writing trick, such as a simile | A tool for cutting paper | A type of bath | A kind of computer game
test: «Leave someone to their own devices» means | *Let them do what they like | Give them a present | Ask them to help you | Make them go to bed
test: «A server is a computer that provides a service, such as web pages, videos or a game world; your own device is called the client.» What is your own device called? | A video | A server | *The client | A website
exam: Which sentence uses device to mean a clever trick? | «Devices can switch themselves off when they get too hot.» | *«The poet used a simile as a device to make the sea sound alive.» | «Charging devices outside the bedroom removes the temptation to play at night.» | «Put your devices away at dinner.»
